1. A palindromic path reads the same forwards and backwards
2. I can build palindromes from the middle outward
3. For even-length palindromes, the middle is a single vertex
4. For odd-length palindromes, the middle is an edge

I'll use BFS starting from all possible "middles" and expand outward by adding matching characters to both ends until I reach the desired start and end vertices.

